[require map::box::map-display [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides an engine attachable to a [package map::display] widget, extending the map's
behaviour. The engine shows a set of [term geo/box] definitions taken from a store on the map,
each as a canvas rectangle managed by a [package canvas::edit::rectangle] instance (used for display only, not for
editing).

It tracks the visible part of the map, ensuring that only the visible boxes use canvas
resources (items).

[section {Class API}]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::box::map-display] [arg objectName] [arg map] [arg store] [opt "[arg option] [arg value]..."]]
[call [cmd {::map box map-display}] [arg objectName] [arg map] [arg store] [opt "[arg option] [arg value]..."]]

This command creates a new engine named [arg objectName], attaches it to the [package map::display]
widget [arg map], and returns the fully qualified name of the object command. The name
[const %AUTO%] generates a unique name.

[para] The engine starts disabled, i.e. it shows nothing until its method [method enable] is
called.

[para] The [arg store] is a command prefix providing the boxes to show, with the API of
[package map::box::store::memory]. The engine uses its methods [method visible] to query the boxes in the
visible part of the map, [method get] for the keys [const geo] (the box) and [const center] of their attributes, and
[method pixels] for their location on the map, a [term pointbox]. The store is invoked at the global
level.

[para] The engine attaches to the map by chaining the option [option -on-view-change] of the
widget, see the section [emph {Attaching behaviours}] in the manpage of [package map::display].
[list_end]

[section Options]

All options can only be set at creation time.

The appearance options, if specified, are passed to the [package canvas::edit::rectangle] instances;
when not specified, the defaults of that package apply.

[list_begin options]
[opt_def -on-active [arg command-prefix]]

A command prefix invoked at the global level, with the id of a box as additional argument,
whenever the mouse pointer enters the outline of a box. Leaving it is not reported.

The result of the command is ignored. The default is the empty string, i.e. no reporting.

[opt_def -color [arg color]]

The color of the boxes.

[opt_def -hilit-color [arg color]]

The color of a box while the mouse pointer is over it.

[opt_def -rect-config [arg list]]

A list of options and their values applied to the canvas rectangle items, see [package canvas::edit::rectangle].

[opt_def -kind [arg itemtype]]
[opt_def -create-cmd [arg command-prefix]]

The appearance of the markers shown at the corner points of the boxes, see
[package canvas::edit::rectangle].

[opt_def -radius [arg integer]]

The radius of the default markers shown at the corner points.

The engine always sets the radius of the default corner markers to [const 0], hiding them,
so setting this option has no visible effect.
[list_end]

[section Methods]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg objectName] [method enable]]

This method enables the engine: it shows the boxes in the visible part of the map and from now
on follows changes of the visible part. Enabling an enabled engine does nothing.

The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method disable]]

This method disables the engine: it removes all boxes from the map and stops following the
changes of the visible part. Disabling a disabled engine does nothing.

The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method focus] [arg id]]

This method moves the map so that the box with the given [arg id] is at its center, and
chooses the largest zoom level at which the whole box is visible.

The result of the method is the empty string.

[call [arg objectName] [method destroy]]

This method disables the engine, detaches it from the map, and destroys it.
[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

Showing the boxes read from the [file *.box] files in directory [file boxes]:

[example {
package require map::display
package require map::provider::osm
package require map::box::store::fs
package require map::box::store::memory
package require map::box::map-display

file mkdir tiles
set provider [map provider osm %AUTO% tiles]
map display .map -provider $provider -initial-geo {48.137 11.575} -initial-zoom 10
pack .map -fill both -expand 1

map box store fs     files  boxes
map box store memory store  files
map box map-display  layer  .map store -on-active puts
layer enable
}]

